    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0361" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1404.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé White to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-14T16:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dominican Government summoned me this morning to state that the revolutionists
                    are also in possession of Jaina. Dominican Government stated that its national
                    line of defense in extremities was city walls but that in view of safety of
                    suburban foreign population it desired to confer with me re restriction of area.
                    I had told them that without instructions I did not propose to submit matter to
                    action Diplomatic Corps. I advised them that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Castine</hi> would permit no firing by Government or revolutionary forces
                    within the limits of the city and that should they be unable to stave off rebels
                    unaided they had better request good offices of American Government for the
                    solution of whole question. Dominican Government replied that they would rather
                    resign than do this but were willing to ask assistance from Washington for
                    overcoming rebels and were also agreeable to establishment of neutral zone,
                    quoting Puerto Plata as a precedent. Pending instructions from Washington <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Castine</hi> will enforce neutral zone but I would
                    respectfully suggest to Department that the situation lends itself to
                    comprehensive treatment. Savinon has postponed trip to Puerto Plata. Another war
                    vessel and particularly marines would be appreciated.</p>
                <closer>[Not signed.] [<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed>.]</closer>
            </div>
